.TH DSPAMINFO 8
.SH NAME
dspaminfo \- Diablo program to show or clear the internal spam filter cache
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dspaminfo
.B \-l
[
.B \-r
]
.br
.B dspaminfo
.B \-c
.I n
.PP
[
.B \-B
]
[
.B \-N
]
[
.BR \-d [\fIn\fP]
]
[
.B \-C
.I diablo.config
]
[
.B \-V
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Diablo's internal spam filter (the
.B internalfilter
setting in diablo.config) keeps two caches in shared memory: one of
article bodies (the body filter) and one of posting hosts (the NNTP
posting host, "nph", filter).
.I dspaminfo
prints their entries or clears them, for example to release a host that
was caught by mistake.  One of
.B \-l
or
.B \-c
is required.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-l
Print the cache entries.
.TP
.B \-r
With \fB\-l\fP, also print expired entries.
.TP
.BI \-c " n"
Clear entry \fIn\fP (the number shown by \fB\-l\fP), or all entries if
\fIn\fP is \-1.
.TP
.B \-B
Work on the body filter cache.
.TP
.B \-N
Work on the posting host cache.
.PP
\-l without \-B or \-N shows both caches; \-c needs one or both.
.TP
.BR \-d [\fIn\fP]
Set the debug level.
.TP
.BI \-C " diablo.config"
Use this diablo.config instead of the default.
.TP
.B \-V
Print the version and exit.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
diablo(8),
dicmd(8),
diablo-files(5)
